---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy — Atlas">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-muted">Last updated: July 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-text leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">What we collect</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">When you sign in with GitHub OAuth, we store your GitHub username, email, and avatar URL. We do not collect or store your GitHub password.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">How we use your data</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">Your email is used to send daily digests if you opt in. Your GitHub profile is used to personalize your news scoring. We do not sell or share your data with third parties.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Cookies</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">We use a single httpOnly session cookie for authentication. No tracking cookies, no analytics cookies (unless you opt into PostHog).</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Data retention</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">Your account data is retained until you delete your account. Digest history is retained for 30 days. You can request deletion by contacting us on GitHub.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Third-party services</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">Atlas uses GitHub OAuth for authentication, Groq and Gemini for AI scoring, and Resend for email delivery. Each service has its own privacy policy.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">Questions? Open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/pantha704/atlas">GitHub</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
